ial-failure error, which left the service mixed across regions. A second rollback to v2.3.0 completed in all regions.\n- **Version choice:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and the partial failure. On-call has been paged. The first incident request timed out, so I retried with the same idempotency key, and the incident was created once.\n\nFollow-up for the team: find the cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure. Don't redeploy v2.3.1 or v2.3.1-rc until they're fixed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01ARtRoAYkssu1y3jmtBPS2j", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01ANfwcgsRZiD7sSknF6KqK9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The current release is v2.3.1, which is unhealthy. The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0, which has run healthy in production, so it doesn't need change-manager approval. I'll roll back to it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Cq7gZgFvouS5GK17eAQaVJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback reported a partial failure after us-east. I'll check the current state before doing anything else.", "type": "tex